{"kind":"report","text":"Approved as the requested DESIGN outline and five-stage acceptance plan at exact4d1a05fd2637183ac66906d1008e41e915c49a69, tree0a584a12602cbd962b95b8a2c422231853b383ed. The sole examined/reporting artifact is3046c54d. No blocking contradiction was established for this planning scope. The explicit decisions of section9 remain prerequisites to a separately commissioned connector contract/implementation; this approval closes no import runtime, provider, P1 bottleneck, archive or complete capacity duty.\n\nArchitecture: the note correctly separates native import ownership/adoption from Git transfer, directory indexing from issue history, and GitHub synchronization from native receipt semantics. Source confirms the missing production import owner (artifacts-wiring93-100 handles register/destination only), whole-closure objects path (artifacts-host194-207, Reader.closure283-312), original issue/member/comment limits and signer semantics, and replay's incomplete result for unavailable retained inputs (verify564-573). The proposal's R2 resolver is explicitly new work, with a byte-domain/digest/size/ownership contract and no cross-service atomicity assumption. Directory lifetime and complete consumer pagination stay with separately commissioned P1 work; moving rows or archiving history does not renew a100000-entry lifetime. Native version/pin changes and current room migration remain explicit.\n\nSecurity: imported authors remain source attestations by a repository-bound synchronizer; external identities gain no dap keys or grants. Private input visibility and publication rights require explicit bridge policy. Webhook HMAC, delivery/source deduplication, durable acknowledgement, loss reconciliation and separate Unknown states are sound design boundaries. Marker matching is correlation rather than authority; no blind POST retry or inferred exactly-once claim is present. An external close cannot substitute for native completion guards. Git ref CAS/divergence, owned cleanup and secret custody are correctly separated from source repository deletion.\n\nSimplification: retain the existing judgments, signed acts, receipts, native delivery settlement and immutable Git identities. The coordinator should hold orchestration/mappings, not become a second issue-authority database. Workflows/Queues carry durable work identifiers rather than correctness state. R2 addresses large evidence with explicit resolver work, while repositories above Artifacts limits remain unsupported or require an explicit reduced-history choice. No custom Git backend or ordinary-blob pointer rewrite is assumed. All five stages remain required.\n\nKeep these concrete choices in the required pre-implementation contract review (section9 already gates them):\n- Bind each local issue result to its outbound duty through that scope's native transaction/outbox, then use replayable idempotent delivery to the coordinator. Two DO commits cannot implement one atomic local-act-plus-coordinator-outbox write. Define stale revisions/echoes/overlapping local operations and the final bridge/installation permission checks, including revocation of queued writes.\n- Specify the bootstrap selection and convergence rule for issues closing/reopening while open-only pages shift; dedup alone does not establish completeness. Bind each complete observation to a census/window and require the comment edit/deletion pass too. Keep catch-up visible when convergence is not proved.\n- Choose the initial mutable-field publication policy with the acknowledged unsafe-write race. An explicit human confirmation or re-read cannot eliminate the final GitHub read/PATCH race; do not promote it into an atomic compare-and-swap claim.\n- Define retained capture byte domains, redaction/tombstone ownership and archive omissions before exporting raw API JSON or attachment bytes. An immutable capture containing deleted text cannot be erased by changing only displayed text. Restricted/missing evidence must preserve its honest verification result. Also fix tracked-ref policy, source revision ordering, workload/partition identity and the operator path for an irreducibly Unknown write before their dependent code.\n\nPrimary-document checks support the note's key external boundaries: Artifacts1GB/32MB and request limits (https://developers.cloudflare.com/artifacts/platform/limits/); public HTTPS import, explicit branch/depth and in-progress409 (https://developers.cloudflare.com/artifacts/guides/import-repositories/); SQL10GB/2MB (https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/platform/limits/); issue pagination/pull_request filtering (https://docs.github.com/en/rest/issues/issues); failed webhooks are not automatically redelivered (https://docs.github.com/en/webhooks/using-webhooks/handling-failed-webhook-deliveries); and unsafe conditional writes are unsupported unless specifically documented (https://docs.github.com/en/rest/using-the-rest-api/best-practices-for-using-the-rest-api). These are documentation checks, not observed provider behavior or measured workloads.\n\nValidation: the complete372-line note was read, with selected cited native/source context and primary platform documentation. Native diff from parent/Main0157307b904c9afc75500b626fc565a152113cfa (tree57a85a9cfe99e07d9de660900986f597533e88fb) names only this note; whitespace check passed. The exact public projection granted byecd32997 was checked as an owned regular file,1648bytes,SHA256045fff1a395a3c982c6185888be3128abeb808ae75b4b08641de0ea2dc93986d. It binds unchanged start/end head/tree and a clean checkout, one FAILED gate exit1: install/whitespace/typecheck passed;1230Vitest passed,1failed,3skipped; hosted H5/H6/H7 line338 expected ': stream' and got empty text; downstream Node/browser groups did not run. Failure cause is unestablished; runtime/tests/lock are unchanged. This approval carries that failed-gate qualification and no runtime gate pass. Checker ran no project code, tests, gate, connector/provider operation or private/nested evidence reads and changed no source.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3046c54d0caa8597ac063db0902e60cd9fb54a31","binding":"assigned","head":"4d1a05fd2637183ac66906d1008e41e915c49a69","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9d8e67899510caaa98e43262e0d46a554c91e97d\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f4bbdac24168094d1acb822adc338ba3a45d2e86\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6aa3bc30a12bee111c1aecc1735a5527d0585116","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}